WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.110
We recently put out a video on 10 mistakes
you should avoid when buying a new 2019 MacBook

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.969
Pro, and you guys liked it so much that you
asked us to do the same thing for the new

00:00:08.969 --> 00:00:10.760
iMac, so here it is.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.759
Here are # Mistakes to avoid when buying a
new 2019 iMac.

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:19.080
For Mistake #1, do NOT buy the cheap $1100
iMac option.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.080
EVER.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.710
No one should buy this model, not even people
on a budget.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:29.170
You only get a 1080P display, a slow 7th gen
dual-core processor, slower RAM, and integrated

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.170
graphics.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.070
It’s basically the worst choice you can
ever make in an iMac.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.940
Paying an extra $200 gets you a much more
capable machine with a much better display.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.880
But even then, I would recommend at least
the $1500 4K iMac because it gets a 6-core

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.149
processor and a dedicated graphics card with
4GB of video memory.

00:00:47.149 --> 00:00:51.470
If you’re looking to buy a very cheap iMac
for around $1100, you should instead buy a

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:57.670
discounted 2017 model like this one, which
packs a 4K display, quad-core processor and

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.240
faster graphics for $450 off.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.980
We’ll link it down below.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:07.020
For Mistake #2, Do not buy an iMac with either
a hard drive or a fusion drive.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.930
First of all, hard drives are incredibly slow
and they’re more prone to failure compared

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.670
to other storage solutions.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:18.080
Fusion drives combine a large hard drive with
a small SSD, for example, only 24gigs of SSD

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.390
for this 1TB fusion drive.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.100
This does speed it up a bit, but it still
has the same reliability issues.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.020
Now an SSD is like a high-speed flash drive,
it has no moving parts so it’s more reliable.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.180
Not only that, but it’s MUCH faster than
any hard drive or fusion drive, and it’s

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.119
only a $100 upgrade for most configurations.

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:42.159
We’d recommend getting at least 512GB, but
even the 256gig SSD is a much better choice

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.130
than the 1TB fusion drive.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:49.810
And worst case scenario, you can buy a portable
1TB hard drive for just $45 on Amazon for

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.439
long-term storage and backups.

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:56.990
Now onto Mistake #3, if you’re buying a
27-inch model, do not pay for the RAM upgrade.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.530
Keep it at 8GB.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:02.340
Most people know this already, but this iMac
features a user-accessible RAM door on the

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.900
back, allowing you to upgrade the RAM yourself.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.920
It’s incredibly simple and it doesn’t
void your warranty.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.400
We even made a step-by-step guide that you
can follow to do it yourself, and we’ll

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.760
put a button on the end of this video that
links to it.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.700
There are four RAM slots, and Apple uses up
two for the factory 8GB of RAM, and yes, you

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.220
can add two more sticks and leave Apple’s
RAM in there and it won’t cause any issues.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:29.430
The 64GB upgrade from Apple costs $1,000,
while you can currently buy 64GB of RAM on

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:37.150
Amazon for only $284, that’s $716 saved,
not including the difference in taxes, and

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.280
they’re not any worse than Apple’s RAM.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.470
Trust me, I’ve been using this RAM on my
iMac for the last 2 years.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.340
I’ll leave a link to it down below.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:49.630
For Mistake #4, some high-end users need a
ton of RAM, like for virtualization or high-end

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:55.290
production work, and they mistakenly by Apple’s
maximum listed 64GB RAM option, but it’s

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.950
actually not the max.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:03.599
The new 2019 5K iMac actually supports up
to 128GB of RAM with OWC’s third-party RAM

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:08.629
kit, and the craziest thing about it is that
it’s only $900, that’s $100 less than

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:09.629
Apple’s 64GB kit.

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:12.660
We’ll also leave the link to that below.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.840
This is huge news for people who really need
that much RAM, allowing them to buy an iMac

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.430
instead of going for a more expensive iMac
Pro.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:26.099
For Mistake #5, the smaller 21.5” 4K iMac
does not have user-accessible RAM.

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:29.849
Some people buy this iMac and buy RAM, then
realize that it doesn’t have a RAM door

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:30.849
on the back.

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:32.159
So don’t make that mistake.

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:35.760
If you need a lot of RAM, the 27-inch 5K iMac
is a much better value.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.760
Let’s say you configure the $1500 4K iMac
option with 32GB of RAM.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:37.760
That brings the price up to $2100.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.760
Instead, you can upgrade to the $1800 base
5K iMac and buy 32GB of aftermarket RAM for

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.760
$142, and you can use that in addition to
Apple’s RAM to make it have 40gigs of RAM,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.760
for a total of $1,942 for a much better machine
with a better display and more performance.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.760
Enough with the RAM, let’s move onto Mistake
#6, if you’re a photographer or someone

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.879
who does processor-heavy work, like Logic
Pro or programming, do not upgrade the graphics.

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:47.270
Trust me, you don’t need it.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:51.320
We ran tests in Lightroom and found that upgrading
graphics did literally nothing at all for

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.320
performance.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.099
Instead, put your extra money towards upgrading
the RAM.

00:03:55.099 --> 00:04:01.220
We found that having only 16GB limited performance,
so get at least a 16GB Kit and add it to the

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:06.910
factory 8GB for a total of 24gigs if you’re
on a budget, but we’d recommend the 32Gig

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.019
kit for a total of 40GB to be safe.

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:13.569
Now onto Mistake #7, if you’re a high-end
video editor, the most important thing for

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:19.470
you is the graphics, and the 2019 5K iMac
has a brand new Vega 48 graphics option, but

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:23.849
you have to choose the highest-end 5K iMac
configuration for the option to show up.

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:24.849
The Vega 48 upgrade is $450, but trust us,
it’s worth it.

00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:25.849
Leave the 6-core processor, buy an aftermarket
32gig RAM kit and upgrade to the 512GB SSD

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:26.849
and you’ve got an awesome video editing
machine for just under $3,000.

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:27.849
The reason I say you should leave the 6-core
is because most people won’t see much of

00:04:27.849 --> 00:04:28.849
a difference unless they’re high-end RAW
video footage editors.

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:29.849
In that case, the $400 8-core upgrade is worth
it.

00:04:29.849 --> 00:04:33.039
And if you can’t afford the Vega 48 option,
avoid I’d still recommend the $2300 5K iMac

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:37.139
because it’s the only other one that comes
with a graphics card that has 8GB of video

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:39.139
memory, and that’s very important for video
editing.

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:40.139
For Mistake #8, don’t pay for any processor
upgrade unless it bumps you up from a 4-core

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:41.139
to a 6-core or a 6-core to an 8-core.

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:42.139
Two years ago, i5 processors did not have
hyperthreading, which gives you two CPU threads

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:43.139
per core, greatly increasing performance,
but now, every new i5 has it, just like i7

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:44.139
processors.

00:04:44.139 --> 00:04:45.139
The only real difference is a small speed
boost, which usually isn’t worth the extra

00:04:45.139 --> 00:04:46.139
cost.

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:47.139
Now onto Mistake #9, you may have heard that
the 2019 iMac has Intel’s 9th-gen processor,

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:48.139
but be careful because only the top two configurations
can get the 9th gen processor.

00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:49.139
The $2300 model comes with a 6-core and the
$1999 can be upgraded to an 8-core 9th gen

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:50.139
for $500.

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:51.139
However, we don’t recommend that you make
that upgrade because if you also upgrade the

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:52.139
storage to 512GB, you’ll end up at the same
exact $2800 price for the same specs as the

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:53.139
upgraded $2300 model, except that you’ll
only get the 570X graphics instead of the

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:54.139
better 580X graphics, so just start with the
top-spec $2300 model instead.

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:55.139
And finally, for mistake #10, don’t feel
like you absolutely have to get the 8-core

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:56.139
to get great performance.

00:04:56.139 --> 00:04:57.139
Looking at benchmarks of these new processors,
even the cheapest 3.0GHz 6-core CPU from the

00:04:57.139 --> 00:04:58.139
$1800 model outperforms the best processor
available in the 2017 iMac, which I’ve been

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:00.550
using every day for the past 2 years for video
editing and it’s been more than fast enough

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.909
for the standard 4K editing that we do.

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:06.909
And there you have it, there are 10 mistakes
you should avoid when purchasing a new 2019

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:07.909
iMac.

00:05:07.909 --> 00:05:11.870
You can check out those iMac videos right
there, and If this video helped you out, tap

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.740
like and click that circle above to subscribe.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:19.340
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next one!

